      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Logo Programming Language",
      "url": "https://el.media.mit.edu/logo-foundation/what_is_logo/logo_programming.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/oh5hqw",
      "score": 6,
      "comments": 2,
      "author": "rajtilakjee",
      "published": "2026-09-12T16:04:06Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Developed in 1967 as a Lisp dialect, Logo pioneered educational programming via symbolic computation, list processing, and interactive syntax.",
        "Its turtle graphics system introduced early vector-based spatial abstractions, directly inspiring modern visual environments like MIT Scratch.",
        "Architecturally influenced modern dynamic languages and early GUI paradigms through constructivist principles and first-class procedure support."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Linux Zoom Client Proactively Reads X11 Clipboard",
      "url": "https://hachyderm.io/@simontatham/117201594980991062",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/8t1ddm",
      "score": 34,
      "comments": 15,
      "author": "darleaf",
      "published": "2026-09-12T12:38:53Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Zoom's Linux desktop client continuously inspects X11 clipboard buffers in the background without requiring explicit user paste actions.",
        "Because X11 lacks granular access controls, any background poll can harvest credentials or tokens copied from password managers.",
        "Security teams should migrate users to Wayland or sandbox Zoom via Flatpak to enforce strict clipboard isolation."
      ]
    },
